<report>
<title>Kendall's rank correlation</title>

<p>@sample_1 vs. @sample_2<br />
Observations per sample = @obs<br />
Concordant pairs = @con<br />
Discordant pairs = @dis<br />
Tied pairs = @tie<br />
Kendall's score = @s   (standard error = @{ses:roundu})<br />
Gamma = @{gam:roundu}</p>

<p>Kendall's @tb = @{tau:roundu}<br />
<ci>Approximate @{pc:round2}% CI = @{ll:roundu} to @{ul:roundu}</ci></p>

<p><u>Approximate tests@adj</u></p>
<block name="smallsample">
<p><warn>Sample size too small for reliable inference from z, use exact test</warn></p>
</block>
<p>z = @{kz:roundu}<br />
<pval>Upper side @{p_u:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)<br />
<pval>Lower side @{p_l:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)<br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</p>

<p>z (continuity corrected) = @{kzcc:roundu}<br />
<pval>Upper side @{p_ucc:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)<br />
<pval>Lower side @{p_lcc:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)<br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2cc:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</p>

<p><u>Exact test@adjexact</u><br />
<pval>Upper side @{p_uexact:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: concordance)<br />
<pval>Lower side @{p_lexact:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: discordance)<br />
<pval>Two sided @{p_2exact:pval}</pval>  (H<sub>1</sub>: dependence)</p>
</report>
